\subsection{Source-Reachable Path Lyapunov Certificate}
\label{sec:stability-widening-source-path}

The quantitative Live certificate is built only on jointly source-reachable
execution words.  The compact envelope of Sec.~\ref{sec:stability-widening-phase-a}
remains useful for existence, boundedness, and adaptation-law independence, but
it is not used as a second quantitative certificate route.  Likewise, the
certificate below does not introduce a common Euclidean contraction test, a
common quadratic metric, a repeated one-step contraction construction, or a
one-step nonlinear alternative.

The translational qualification of every quantitative word uses the
source-cadence-only complete-chain route of Lemma~\ref{lem:iss-axis-uco}: four
usable $S=0$ updates observe $(v,p,S,a_w)$.  Equation~\eqref{eq:iss-S-spread-index}
defines $q_W$ as the largest spread index guaranteed to fit in the word.  The
same determinant proof is valid for every integer $q$ with
$1\le q\le q_W$, using rows
$t_0,t_q,t_{2q},t_{3q}$ and the factor
$(q\Delta_{S,-})^6$.  A quantitative certificate therefore need not choose the
largest geometric spread blindly.  It evaluates every admissible integer $q$
with validated arithmetic and selects
\begin{equation}
 q_W^*\in\arg\max_{1\le q\le q_W}
 \underline\lambda_{S,W}(q),
 \label{eq:widen-optimal-S-spread}
\end{equation}
where $\underline\lambda_{S,W}(q)>0$ is the rigorous information-Gramian lower
bound after the corresponding OU-decay and row-norm penalties are included.
Thus the proof credits all available separation while avoiding a longer spread
when its additional OU decay or conditioning would reduce the certified lower
bound.  This discrete proof-design optimization uses only source bounds and is
not trajectory fitting.

The three-$S$ integrator detectability construction remains useful for a
different purpose.  Together with the uniform exponential stability of the
omitted $a_w$ direction it can sharpen a Riccati/covariance upper bound without
reconstructing $a_w$ through the exponentially small four-point determinant.
It does not replace the four-$S$ complete-observability qualification and is not
a theorem-promotion fallback.  The separate three-$S$ coupled observability
route of Lemma~\ref{lem:iss-three-s-coupled} may be used as a full-observability
argument only when its independent conditional latent-acceleration information
hypothesis is itself certified on the same source word.

The homogeneous held-bias and active-bias systems have different active
coordinates (18 and 21 states).  The construction is therefore applied
separately to each fixed-dimensional normal-Live mode
$m\in\{H,A\}$.  Bias release, hard magnetic re-gauging, and tilt re-lock are
explicit source transitions between certified domains rather than fictitious
square-matrix products across different state dimensions.

\subsubsection{Finite source graph and path-dependent linear metric}

For mode $m$, introduce a finite proof graph
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr G_{{\rm src},m}=(\mathscr M_m,\mathscr E_m),
 \label{eq:widen-src-graph}
\end{equation}
whose nodes cover the compact source-reachable proof state in that mode.  Nodes
encode the source quantities that affect the error map, including pseudo-
measurement phase, accepted-update pattern, magnetic state, covariance state,
commit/hold state, and declared compact cells of the scheduled parameters.
Each edge $e=(i,j)\in\mathscr E_m$ carries the compact matrix family
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr A_e:=\left\{
 \widetilde{\mat A}_{k,m}^{\rm cl}:
 \text{the implemented source can move from node $i$ to node $j$}
 \right\}.
 \label{eq:widen-src-edge-family}
\end{equation}
Continuous covariance and tuning values remain continuous variables inside the
edge family; they are not replaced by nominal point samples.

For a graph word
$w=(i_0,e_0,i_1,\ldots,e_{r-1},i_r)$ define the source-correlated matrix family
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr P_w:=\left\{
 \mat\Phi_w=\mat A_{r-1}\cdots\mat A_0:
 \begin{array}{l}
 \mat A_s\in\mathscr A_{e_s},\\
 \text{the complete tuple is jointly source reachable}
 \end{array}
 \right\}.
 \label{eq:widen-src-word-family}
\end{equation}
The joint reachability clause is essential.  Extrema of
$(\tau,\sigma_{aw},r_S,T_S)$ or of gate/covariance state that cannot coexist on
one estimator execution are not multiplied together merely because they lie in
the same Cartesian envelope.  At an arbitrary word entrance, however, the
invariant applied-parameter box is retained unless source history excludes a
combination: the independent $r_S$ smoothing state in particular prevents a
static target-law correlation from being used to delete admissible entrance
corners.  Correlation widening is obtained by propagating the actual source
recurrences inside the word, not by assuming instantaneous algebraic coupling
that the implementation does not enforce.

Let $\mathscr W_{{\rm src},m}$ be a finite collection of words with
\begin{equation}
 1\le\ell_-\le\ell(w)\le\ell_+<\infty.
 \label{eq:widen-src-word-length}
\end{equation}
It is \emph{source complete} when every infinite execution that remains in
mode $m$ can be tiled successively by words in
$\mathscr W_{{\rm src},m}$.

A validated Riccati/information calculation may use any nonsingular
conditioning congruence that is applied to both sides of a generalized matrix
inequality.  Such a congruence is a numerical device and is not automatically
the Lyapunov metric used below.  In particular, a source-varying
$\Sigma_{\rm KF}^{-1}$ or a conditioned $RL^{-1}$ basis may certify a linear
information margin without introducing attitude--linear cross terms into the
nonlinear group energy.

To keep the linear path certificate exactly compatible with the nonlinear
$\SO(3)$ lift below, split the local error coordinate as
$\vct z=(\delta\vct\theta,\vct\xi)$, where $\vct\xi$ contains every
non-attitude coordinate in the fixed-dimensional mode.  For each graph node
choose $a_{R,i}>0$ and a symmetric matrix $\mat P_{\xi,i}\succ0$, and define
the group-compatible local quadratic metric
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \overline{\mat P}_i:=
 \operatorname{blkdiag}\!\left(
       \frac{a_{R,i}}{2}\mat I_3,\mat P_{\xi,i}\right).}
 \label{eq:widen-path-Pbar}
\end{equation}
The coefficient $a_{R,i}/2$ is not an arbitrary restriction: because
$V_R=1-\cos\theta=\tfrac12\|\delta\theta\|^2+O(\|\delta\theta\|^4)$,
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-Pbar} is precisely the local quadratic of the exact
group metric in Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-group-metric}.  No attitude--linear
cross term is admitted that would disappear when the attitude coordinate is
lifted back to $\SO(3)$.  The matrices $P_{\xi,i}$ and weights $a_{R,i}$ may be
optimized node by node; the theorem does not require a common quadratic metric
or equality with the Kalman information matrix.

Require uniform metric bounds
\begin{equation}
 p_-\mat I\preceq\overline{\mat P}_i\preceq p_+\mat I,
 \qquad i\in\mathscr M_m.
 \label{eq:widen-path-P-bounds}
\end{equation}
For every certified word impose the robust path inequality
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mat\Phi_w^\top\overline{\mat P}_{i_r}\mat\Phi_w
 -\overline{\mat P}_{i_0}\preceq-\mat Q_w,
 \qquad
 \mat Q_w\succeq q_w\mat I,
 \quad q_w>0,}
 \label{eq:widen-path-lmi}
\end{equation}
for every $\mat\Phi_w\in\mathscr P_w$.

\begin{theorem}[Source-complete path Lyapunov UES]
\label{thm:widen-path-ues}
For a fixed normal-Live mode $m$, suppose
$\mathscr W_{{\rm src},m}$ is source complete,
Eqs.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-P-bounds}--\eqref{eq:widen-path-lmi} hold over the
complete compact word families, and every source-word prefix has finite matrix
gain.  Then the homogeneous recursion is uniformly exponentially stable on all
source-reachable executions in that mode.  At a word boundary,
\begin{equation}
 V_{i_r}^+\le\lambda_w V_{i_0}^-,
 \qquad
 \lambda_w:=1-\frac{q_w}{p_+}<1,
 \qquad
 V_i(\vct z):=\vct z^\top\overline{\mat P}_i\vct z.
 \label{eq:widen-path-contraction}
\end{equation}
No decrease is required at an individual sample inside the word.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Equation~\eqref{eq:widen-path-lmi} gives
$V_{i_r}^+-V_{i_0}^-\le-q_w\|z^-\|^2\le-(q_w/p_+)V_{i_0}^-$.  Source
completeness tiles every same-mode execution with contracting words of bounded
length.  The compact prefix families bound the intermediate samples, and
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-P-bounds} converts the word-boundary estimate to a
sample-by-sample UES estimate.
\end{proof}

For quantitative use define the exact generalized word gain
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \lambda_w^{\rm gen}:=
 \sup_{\Phi_w\in\mathscr P_w}
 \lambda_{\max}\!\left(
 \overline P_{i_0}^{-1/2}\Phi_w^\top \overline P_{i_r}
 \Phi_w\overline P_{i_0}^{-1/2}\right)<1,}
 \label{eq:widen-path-generalized-gain}
\end{equation}
and the source-prefix amplification
\begin{equation}
 B_{\rm pre}:=
 \sup_{w\in\mathscr W_{{\rm src},m}}
 \sup_{0\le s<\ell(w)}
 \sup_{\Phi_{w,s}}
 \left\|\overline P_{i_s}^{1/2}\Phi_{w,s}
              \overline P_{i_0}^{-1/2}\right\|<\infty,
 \label{eq:widen-path-prefix}
\end{equation}
where the last supremum is restricted to complete jointly source-reachable
prefixes.  Individual $\lambda_w$ and reachable products are retained as long
as possible; replacing them prematurely by powers of a global worst-word
factor is not part of the certificate.

\subsubsection{Exact group/path nonlinear metric}

Using the same $a_{R,i}$ and $\mat P_{\xi,i}$ as in
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-Pbar}, define
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_i(\mat R_e,\vct\xi)
 :=a_{R,i}V_R(\mat R_e)+\vct\xi^\top\mat P_{\xi,i}\vct\xi.}
 \label{eq:widen-path-group-metric}
\end{equation}
Thus the linear and nonlinear certificates use one group-compatible metric
geometry rather than independently optimized quadratic and group metrics.  The
node domain $\mathcal D_i$ uses a certified geodesic chart
$\theta_e\le\theta_{*,i}<\pi$ together with the source covariance,
measurement, and state bounds.  No Euclidean attitude-radius replacement is
made.

For a word $w:i_0\to i_r$ let
\begin{equation}
 (\mat R_e^+,\vct\xi^+)
 =\mathcal F_w(\mat R_e,\vct\xi,\vct d)
 \label{eq:widen-path-nonlinear-lift}
\end{equation}
be the exact lifted source map.  It composes prediction, all accepted vector
corrections, the full $S=0$ attitude cross-gain, exact quaternion injection,
covariance reset and propagation, source parameter evolution, and every
same-mode guard along the word.

For compact node domains whose complete word prefixes remain safe, define the
zero-input word dissipation margin
\begin{equation}
 \mu_W:=
 \inf_{m}\inf_{w\in\mathscr W_{{\rm src},m}}
 \inf_{\substack{e\in\mathcal D_{i_0}\\e\ne0\\
                  \text{all prefixes safe}}}
 \frac{W_{i_0}(e)-W_{i_r}(\mathcal F_w(e,0))}
 {V_R(\mat R_e)+\|\vct\xi\|^2}.
 \label{eq:widen-path-direct-margin}
\end{equation}
The exact finite-correction identity of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-energy-change} is used inside
$\mathcal F_w$; the attitude contribution is therefore not replaced by a local
Taylor remainder.  The final certificate is on the complete source-correlated
word endpoint, not on a product of independently certified one-sample margins.

\begin{theorem}[Source-word large-angle practical ISS]
\label{thm:widen-path-direct-iss}
Suppose the source graph is complete in each fixed-dimensional normal-Live mode,
all word prefixes remain in their certified domains, and
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\mu_W>0.}
 \label{eq:widen-path-direct-condition}
\end{equation}
Then sufficiently small endpoint sublevels of $W_i$ are robustly invariant for
sufficiently small bounded deterministic input, every intermediate sample stays
inside the declared source domain, and the complete same-mode execution obeys a
practical-ISS estimate.  Positive one-sample changes of $W_i$ are allowed
inside a word.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Condition~\eqref{eq:widen-path-direct-condition} gives strict exact endpoint
decrease for every source word.  On the compact prefix-safe family the lifted
map is uniformly Lipschitz in the bounded deterministic input, including the
small series-branch injection defect.  Young inequalities preserve a strict
inward endpoint margin for a sufficiently small input budget.  Iteration over
the source-complete tiling gives practical ISS at word boundaries and
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-prefix} supplies the sample-prefix bound.
\end{proof}

Dimension-changing or hard-reset transitions are certified by their exact jump
maps between the corresponding node domains.  In particular, held-to-active
bias release must map a certified held-mode sublevel into an active-mode node
sublevel; magnetic re-gauging and tilt re-lock use the hybrid jump conditions of
Sec.~\ref{sec:hybrid-live-stability}.  A tilt reset does not charge discarded
pre-reset tilt energy in its multiplicative gain, and cooldown contraction is
formed from reachable word products rather than a power of a global worst-word
factor.  No square homogeneous transition is formed across a state-dimension
change.

\subsubsection{Verification contract}

A rigorous deployed Live certificate reports
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \{\mathscr G_{{\rm src},m},\mathscr W_{{\rm src},m},
 P_{\xi,i},a_{R,i},\theta_{*,i},\lambda_w^{\rm gen},B_{\rm pre},
 \mu_W\}_{m\in\{H,A\}}.}
 \label{eq:widen-path-contract}
\end{equation}
The pass conditions are: every reachable same-mode transition is covered; the
word family is source complete; the optimized four-$S$ complete-chain and
recurring vector-PE hypotheses are realized inside each tile; all robust matrix
and exact nonlinear word bounds cover the complete continuous jointly
source-reachable family; every prefix is safe; all dimension-changing jumps
enter a certified destination domain; and the relevant word margins are strict.
Interval arithmetic, affine arithmetic, Taylor models, branch-and-bound, robust
LMIs over certified matrix families, or another validated enclosure method may
be used.  Monte Carlo and dense trajectory sampling are diagnostics only and do
not establish the required suprema or infima.

This is the sole quantitative normal-Live certificate path used by the widened
theory.  Older scalar, common-Euclidean, three-$S$ promotion substitutes, or
repeated one-step alternatives are not promotion fallbacks.  The construction
changes neither the estimator nor the adaptation law.
